### E-commerce Microservices Test File
### Use with VS Code REST Client extension or cURL

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080

### 1. Health Check
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

###

### 2. Create Order - Check Stock Available
POST {{baseUrl}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "product_id": "PROD001",
  "quantity": 5,
  "customer_id": "CUST001"
}

###

### 3. Create Order - Check Another Product
POST {{baseUrl}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "product_id": "PROD002",
  "quantity": 3,
  "customer_id": "CUST002"
}

###

### 4. Create Order - Insufficient Stock (will fail)
POST {{baseUrl}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "product_id": "PROD001",
  "quantity": 500,
  "customer_id": "CUST003"
}

###

### 5. Get Order Status (replace ORDER_ID with actual order ID)
GET {{baseUrl}}/orders/ORD-1234567890

###

### cURL Commands for Testing

# Health Check
# curl -X GET http://localhost:8080/health

# Create Order
# curl -X POST http://localhost:8080/orders \
#   -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
#   -d '{"product_id":"PROD001","quantity":5,"customer_id":"CUST001"}'

# Get Order
# curl -X GET http://localhost:8080/orders/ORD-1234567890

### gRPC Testing with grpcurl
# Install grpcurl: https://github.com/fullstorydev/grpcurl

# Check Stock
# grpcurl -plaintext -d '{"product_id":"PROD001","quantity":5}' \
#   localhost:50051 ecommerce.InventoryService/CheckStock

# Track Order (streaming)
# grpcurl -plaintext -d '{"order_id":"ORD-1234567890"}' \
#   localhost:50051 ecommerce.InventoryService/TrackOrder

### RabbitMQ Management UI
# http://localhost:15672
# Username: guest
# Password: guest
